  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 27. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 完了 — 必要なことが全部終わること。\n2. 還暦 — 数え年で六十一歳を迎えること。今は満六十歳で祝うことが多いよ。\n3. カーソル — 画面で文字を入れる位置などを示す印。\n4. カート — 物を載せて押して運ぶ小さな車。\n5. カード — 情報や絵などを載せた小さな札。\n6. カーニバル — 行列や踊りなどでにぎわう祭り。\n7. カーフェリー — 車を載せて人といっしょに運ぶ船。\n8. カーペット — 床に敷く厚手の布。\n9. 外気 — 外の空気。\n10. 外国語 — 外国で使われている言語。\n11. 骸骨 — 体を支える骨組みだけになったもの。\n12. 外出 — 家などから外へ出掛けること。\n13. 外食 — 家庭の外の店などで食事をすること。\n14. 街灯 — 道路などを照らすために立てられた明かり。\n15. ガイドブック — 旅行先や活動の情報を案内する本。\n16. 外壁 — 建物の外側の壁。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
